177
00:11:30.781 --> 00:11:36.285
Price-time priority: best price first, then earliest arrival within a price level (FIFO).

178
00:11:36.565 --> 00:11:39.424
Some markets use pro-rata allocation at a level.

179
00:11:39.704 --> 00:11:40.707
The structures:

180
00:11:40.987 --> 00:11:42.864
Price levels are indexed by tick.

181
00:11:43.144 --> 00:11:49.693
Prices live on a grid inside a band, so an array works, with a tree as a fallback for out-of-band prices.

182
00:11:49.973 --> 00:11:51.957
Each level has a FIFO of orders.

183
00:11:52.237 --> 00:11:58.829
An id, then order map gives O(1) cancel, with intrusive doubly-linked lists for O(1) unlink.

184
00:12:00.179 --> 00:12:02.718
Best-bid and best-ask pointers are maintained.

185
00:12:02.998 --> 00:12:07.457
Identical outputs prove the rules, not the structures, define the result.

186
00:12:07.737 --> 00:12:13.710
That is also how to test a faster book: diff its trade stream against a simple reference implementation.

187
00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:15.035
Tails matter.

188
00:12:15.315 --> 00:12:19.966
A slow operation delays every order behind it in a single-threaded engine.

189
00:12:20.246 --> 00:12:27.649
Avoid allocation and GC on the hot path (object pools, primitive collections), and avoid unbounded scans.

190
00:12:27.929 --> 00:12:30.169
B1's cancel was a linear scan.

191
00:12:31.519 --> 00:12:34.697
Determinism: sequencer, journal, single writer.

