A gap means stale: stop trusting the book and recover.

290
00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:31.357
Recovery: a retransmit service for small gaps, and snapshots (periodic, or on request) for big gaps and late joiners.

291
00:17:31.637 --> 00:17:33.088
Real feeds use both.

292
00:17:33.368 --> 00:17:42.285
Conflation for slow consumers (send the latest state, not every change) and backpressure handling: never let one slow subscriber slow the engine.

293
00:17:42.565 --> 00:17:51.312
Transport: multicast on exchange networks, WebSockets or SSE for apps (Ch 03) with the same sequencing discipline.

294
00:17:52.662 --> 00:17:54.262
Order types and lifecycle.

295
00:17:54.542 --> 00:18:10.713
Limit (rests if not fully matched), market (matches against the book; unfilled remainder cancelled or protected by a price band), IOC or FOK, cancel or replace (replacing loses time priority if the price or size increases, per the rules).

296
00:18:10.993 --> 00:18:20.166
Auctions: a call auction at the open (collect orders, compute a single clearing price that maximises volume) avoids a chaotic first second.

297
00:18:20.446 --> 00:18:22.451
It suits a morning produce market well.

298
00:18:22.731 --> 00:18:30.646
Trade events feed settlement (payment from the buyer's credit line, delivery instructions for the seller) through the ledger (Ch 45).

299
00:18:31.996 --> 00:18:33.959
Latency engineering in Java.

300
00:18:34.239 --> 00:18:38.356
A single-threaded hot loop pinned to a core, avoiding context switches.

301
00:18:38.636 --> 00:18:46.487
No allocation on the hot path (pre-allocated order objects, primitive maps, off-heap buffers), so GC stays quiet.

302
00:18:46.767 --> 00:18:49.689
Otherwise use a low-pause collector (ZGC).

303
00:18:49.969 --> 00:18:57.521
Lock-free single-producer or single-consumer ring buffers between stages (LMAX Disruptor) instead of BlockingQueue.

304
00:18:57.801 --> 00:18:59.849
Measure with HDR histograms.

305
00:19:00.129 --> 00:19:07.233
Report p99.9 and max, not averages, and use coordinated-omission-aware load generators.

306
00:19:08.583 --> 00:19:12.359
Most end-to-end latency is network and gateway, not matching.

307
00:19:12.639 --> 00:19:14.197
Optimise the right stage.

308
