K2) central risk service, synchronous call per order 0 0 rupees138.3 ms 4,000 (0.25 ms. each).

475
00:32:44.276 --> 00:32:56.649
K3) in the sequenced engine path, in-memory exposure 0 0 rupees2 µs not the limit. then a check against a cached number is a check against the past: a buyer spraying.

476
00:32:56.929 --> 00:32:58.444
The rest is in the chapter.

477
00:33:01.294 --> 00:33:02.147
Reading it:

478
00:33:02.427 --> 00:33:08.123
Cached checks let 392 accounts through, with overspends up to about 2 lakh rupees.

479
00:33:08.403 --> 00:33:15.657
The central service is exact, but at bursts its queue becomes latency (138 ms p99).

480
00:33:15.937 --> 00:33:18.006
The in-path check is exact and cheap.

481
00:33:18.286 --> 00:33:20.825
Its latency is an assumed in-process cost.

482
00:33:22.175 --> 00:33:23.433
A development note.

483
00:33:23.713 --> 00:33:29.815
The first calibration pushed 5,000 orders per second at a service capped at 4,000 per second.

484
00:33:30.095 --> 00:33:35.108
That made K2 look broken on average rather than at bursts, so the load was reduced.

485
00:33:36.458 --> 00:33:39.295
L4, Market data that can't lie silently.

486
00:33:39.575 --> 00:33:40.514
Requirement:

487
00:33:40.794 --> 00:33:44.293
Every subscriber's book is either correct or visibly stale.

488
00:33:44.573 --> 00:33:49.010
500k deltas to 200 subscribers, with bursty loss.

489
00:33:50.360 --> 00:33:53.581
Here is the Java code, MarketDataL4.java.

490
00:33:53.861 --> 00:33:57.616
It runs to 93 lines; the full listing is in the chapter.

491
00:33:57.896 --> 00:34:05.832
MarketDataL4.java, run with: java MarketDataL4.java (JDK 21, no dependencies).

492
00:34:06.112 --> 00:34:07.307
PUBLISHING THE BOOK.

493
00:34:07.587 --> 00:34:19.021
The engine emits 500,000 incremental updates (price level P now has size S, 20 bytes each) for. one produce contract over ~5 minutes (fixed seed).

494
00:34:19.301 --> 00:34:23.781
200 subscribers (buyer apps, seller dashboards, risk) receive them.

495
00:34:26.631 --> 00:34:27.549
On screen:

496
00:34:27.829 --> 00:34:45.365
500,000 book updates in ~5 min to 200 subscribers; ~0.1% loss per subscriber in bursts. of 1 to 20. feed design books wrong time with a time knowingly MB sent per. at the end WRONG. book stale. subscriber.

497
